[h1]HWMP Patch 2.4.5 - Cataclysm (Field Test)[/h1]
Shared fixes and original four races for Homeworld Remastered, based on the complete Players Patch 2.3Test build21.
Use this standalone package by itself; do not add another Players Patch.
Workshop release is a field-test candidate.

[h2]New in 2.4.5: Cataclysm Support Units mode[/h2]
Choose [b]HWMP 2.4.5 Cataclysm[/b] under [b]Game Type[/b] in the skirmish/multiplayer setup. The ordinary HWMP modes remain available in the same mod.

Inspired by Homeworld: Cataclysm, this optional mode replaces combat and economy class caps with one weighted Support Units (SU) pool. Mix your fleet freely within that shared budget.
[list]
[*] Four existing races: Hiigaran, Vaygr, Kushan and Taiidan; no additional race selection or separate mod required.
[*] Starting SU budgets: Small 1450; Normal 1900; Large 2600; Huge 3850; Vast 7650.
[*] SU prices in construction, tooltips and selected-ship descriptions; the total counter sits below Resource Units.
[*] Existing carrier/shipyard count caps remain. Carriers do not add capacity. Zero-SU probes keep their classic per-type caps.
[*] A squadron uses its full nominal batch price. The HUD reports owned units and does not include queued construction.
[*] Russian terminology and text encoding fixes; a fourth Kushan emblem in the main menu.
[/list]

[b]Public playtest:[/b] startup and SU display have been checked in-game. Please help test actual build thresholds, simultaneous queues and cancellations, squadron losses/replenishment, capture, saves and two-client synchronization. Balance values are provisional; report the Game Type, Unit Cap, race, observed SU, actions and expected result.

[h2]2.4.1 maintenance update[/h2]
[list]
[*] Removed two stock-identical model copies (Hiigaran mothership and Vaygr Medium missile HODs). 
[*] Both corvette HOD copies remain because shared loading would replace their distinct impact sounds.
[*] Native missile launch/impact checks passed;
[*] Gameplay coefficients are unchanged.
[*] The local main BIG is about 28 MB smaller. Technical filenames stay stable.
[/list]

[h2]Changes[/h2]
[list]
[*] Owner-safe gravity wells, including tested new save/load cases; original permissions/speed are preserved.
[*] Support-frigate cargo recovery, per-ship capture/self-destruct permissions and independent stalled-docking timers.
[*] Refreshed Taiidan missile-defense selections and restored Vaygr Medium missile weapon-fire binding.
[*] Accepted Hgn/Vgr6/6 starting collectors and the Assault Frigate's final speed-accuracy node4 to1.2. Other broad balance coefficients are preserved.
[*] Native build/research tooltip translations for English, French, German, Italian, Spanish and Russian.
[/list]
[h2]Playtesting needed[/h2]
[list]
[*] Two-client MP synchronization;
[*] normal/2x starts and languages;
[*] visible squadron repair;
[*] paid UI hyperspace/cancel and Guard return;
[*] full Hiigaran versus Vaygr matches with side/map swaps.
[/list]
Report release hashes and reproduction steps.
Old active-well saves made before the new journal are not guaranteed.
Specific engine tests do not certify all campaigns or saved transport states.
